<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moesia Inferior</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lower Moesia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moesia">Moesia</a> Inferior was a Roman province on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, covering present-day northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dobruja">Dobruja</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>. It was created around 86 CE, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/domitian">Domitian</a> divided Moesia, and defended the Danube frontier with legions at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/novae">Novae</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silistra">Durostorum</a> and Troesmis. Greek cities of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast, and garrisons as far as Tyras on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dniester">Dniester</a>, were linked to it. It was reorganised in the late Roman reforms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moesia-inferior.jpg" alt="Moesia Inferior" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:REmpire-Moesia.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
